{
  "id": "possessivartikel",
  "name": "Possessives: mon, ma, mes, ton, ta, son, notre, votre, leur",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "subtitle": "Whose is it? Mon appartement, ta clé, ses enfants. The possessive agrees with the thing you have, not with the owner: sa voiture can be his car or her car. For an owner's name, use de: la voiture de Karim.",
  "briefMarks": ["mon", "ma", "mes", "ton", "ta", "tes", "son", "sa", "ses", "notre", "nos", "votre", "vos", "leur", "leurs", "de"],
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "mon / ma / mes · notre / nos · leur / leurs", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">mon</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">fils</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">ma</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">fille</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">mes</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">enfants</span> · <span class=\"vp-prep\">notre</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">maison</span> → <span class=\"vp-prep\">nos</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">maisons</span>",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "For <em>je, tu, il/elle</em> there are three forms: <strong>mon, ma, mes</strong>, <strong>ton, ta, tes</strong>, <strong>son, sa, ses</strong>. <em>mon / ton / son</em> + masculine: <em>mon livre</em>. <em>ma / ta / sa</em> + feminine: <em>ma clé</em>. <em>mes / tes / ses</em> + plural: <em>mes clés</em>.",
        "tag": "mon, ma, mes"
      },
      {
        "html": "Before a vowel or a silent h, a feminine noun takes <strong>mon, ton, son</strong>: <em>mon amie, mon adresse, ton école, son histoire</em>. Not: <em>ma amie</em>.",
        "tag": "mon amie"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>notre, votre, leur</strong> have one form for masculine and feminine: <em>notre appartement, notre maison</em>. The plural is <strong>nos, vos, leurs</strong>: <em>nos enfants</em>. <em>votre</em> goes with <em>vous</em>, also for one person you say <em>vous</em> to.",
        "tag": "notre, votre, leur"
      },
      {
        "html": "The form agrees with the <strong>thing</strong>, not the owner: <em>Karim a une voiture: <strong>sa</strong> voiture.</em> <em>Léa a un frère: <strong>son</strong> frère.</em> A man and a woman both say <em>son frère</em>.",
        "tag": "Match the thing"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>son, sa, ses</strong> mean “his” or “her”. If it is not clear, use the name: <em>la mère de Léa</em>.",
        "tag": "his or her"
      },
      {
        "html": "French has no <em>'s</em>. Say <strong>the thing + de + the owner</strong>: <em>la voiture de Karim, les enfants de Léa, l'appartement de mes parents</em>. <em>de + le = du</em>: <em>le livre du professeur</em>.",
        "tag": "de for owners"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>ma amie</em> → ✓ <em>mon amie</em>. ✗ <em>Léa et sa mari</em> → ✓ <em>Léa et son mari</em>. ✗ <em>Karim's voiture</em> → ✓ <em>la voiture de Karim</em>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "All the forms",
          "note": "Before a vowel, a feminine noun takes mon, ton, son: mon amie.",
          "head": ["Owner", "masculine", "feminine", "plural"],
          "rows": [
            ["je", "mon", "ma", "mes"],
            ["tu", "ton", "ta", "tes"],
